at "ddd d mmm yyyy"}, "B38>B9" {:src "(chance-of #(<= % promised) finishes)", :name "chance", :format "0%"}, "B38>C1" {:src "\"How many times the plan is worked out. More is steadier, and slower: every change to the tasks works them all out again.\""}, "B38>C2" {:src "\"Tasks with each task's work drawn between its Low and High, afresh in each run. On the sheet each draw shows its mean; select it for its step.\""}, "B38>C3" {:src "\"One run's plan: the Scheduler called with the drawn tasks, so its own steps work it out, and a change to the Scheduler is a change here. On the sheet, the plan at the means.\""}, "B38>C4" {:src "\"The drawn plan's last day, Runs times, each with the work drawn afresh, as a histogram: hover a bar for its days. What it gives.\""}, "B38>C5" {:src "\"Half the runs finish by then (the median).\""}, "B38>C6" {:src "\"Four runs in five finish by then: a date to promise. What it gives.\""}, "B38>C7" {:src "\"Nineteen runs in twenty finish by then.\""}, "B38>C8" {:src "\"Typed: the date the launch was promised for.\""}, "B38>C9" {:src "\"The share of runs finishing on or before the promised date.\""}, "B4" {:src "(MAX scheduler>plan>finish)", :name "forecast", :format "d mmm yyyy"}, "B5" {:src "baseline>as-of", :format "d mmm yyyy"}, "B6" {:src "(IF (ROWS baseline>baseline) (MAX baseline>baseline>finish) \"no baseline yet\")", :name "baseline-finish", :format "d mmm yyyy"}, "B7" {:src "(when (number? baseline-finish) (workdays-after baseline-finish forecast working-calendar>calendar))", :format "0 \"working days late\";0 \"working days early\";\"on time\""}, "B8" {:src "(/ (SUMPRODUCT scheduler>plan>work scheduler>plan>done) (SUM scheduler>plan>work))", :format "0%"}, "B9" {:src "(:spi ev)", :format "0.00"}, "C1" {:src "\"A project plan built from blocks: grids that say what they take and give (a plan, capacity, effort, a load), each reading only its inputs. The host holds the data (resources, tasks, the dates) and binds each block's inputs to it; select a block's cell and the Inspector's Inputs show its bindings. The summary reads the blocks' outputs, never their insides.\""}, "C10" {:src "\"Earned value over what was spent: the Timesheet block's effort, each day at what a day of its task costs.\""}, "C11" {:src "\"Tasks whose forecast finish is after their baseline finish: the Tracking block's output.\""}, "C12" {:src "\"The tasks with no slack.\""}, "C13" {:src "\"Days a resource is booked past what it has, as the Scheduler block's what's left says: below 0 when two tasks share a day. Only when Level resources is off.\""}, "C14" {:src "\"Weeks ahead where a resource has more days booked than the week has working days: read from the load table (below), not from a chart.\""}, "C15" {:src "\"PV, EV and AC summed over the tasks.\""}, "C16" {:src "\"Tasks begun with nobody said to be on them, or with someone on them the task didn't ask for: the plan's who-check, from the Timesheet's people per task.\""}, "C18" {:src "\"The first day of the project.\""}, "C19" {:src "\"The day the actuals are as of. Work not done is scheduled after it.\""}, "C20" {:src "\"Ticked, a resource does one task at a time: tasks wait for it.\""}, "C22" {:src "\"Who does the work: units (1 full time, 0.5 half) and a day rate. Said to be resources (This table is, on the Shelf): blocks taking resources find it.\""}, "C23" {:src "\"What there is to do: work in days, who does it, what it waits for, and the actuals as they come in (Started, Finished, Done). Who: Resource names people or things, Role asks for any one of a role's people (Roles, above), and Follows on gives it whoever got that task (Visual design whoever did the wireframes). Time spent is the Timesheet block's now. Said to be tasks.\""}, "C24" {:src "\"Who can do what: a row per resource per role, so Ana is a designer and a developer. A task's Role is then any one of that role's people, the one finishing first picked. Said to be pools (This table is, on the Shelf): the Scheduler block takes them.\""}, "C26" {:src "\"A block: it takes resources (its Units the first layer), keeps its layers as its own tables, and gives capacity, a calendar. Its layers' Resource columns take any names for now: they aren't checked against the resources it is given.\""}, "C27" {:src "\"A block: rows of who worked on what, when and for how long, typed by the people doing the work. It knows nothing of schedules: it gives effort, by resource, day and task. It takes the tasks, so Task is picked from them with the ▾ and shows each task's name (the cell holds its ID). Resource isn't checked against the sheet's yet.\""}, "C28" {:src "\"A block: the Schedule step over the tasks it takes, into the capacity it takes, from the start and status dates; a task's Role is any one of that role's people, from the pools it takes (the host's Roles), and who is on a task once begun from the effort it takes (the Timesheet's: whoever logged time to it). It gives the plan, its bookings, and what they leave of the calendar.\""}, "C29" {:src "\"A block that keeps named baselines of any table (its input says no concept): type a name and press. It gives the latest as the baseline (bound to the plan, a plan too), and compares any two, or one with the plan now, as a table and as a Gantt.\""}, "C3" {:src "\"The day the actuals are as of (Settings, below).\""}, "C30" {:src "\"A block taking two plans, the plan and its baseline, told apart by what each is bound to; effort by task, which its binding sums from the Timesheet block's effort (by resource, day and task); capacity, for working days; resources' rates; the status date.\""}, "C31" {:src "\"A block: a Gantt chart of the plan it takes, its baseline beneath; click a bar and the task's row of the tasks it takes shows below, to change. Typing there writes into the host's Tasks because the host ticked edit beside that binding (the Inspector's Inputs).\""}, "C32" {:src "\"Each resource's days booked beside its working days, week by week: the host's own table, said to be a load. Both loading blocks take a load and are bound to it: either can replace the other. A sheet without one is offered it, made by a weekly series, when a loading block is placed.\""}, "C33" {:src "\"The first week the load counts.\""}, "C34" {:src "\"How many weeks the load counts.\""}, "C35" {:src "\"A loading view: it takes a load and draws it, week by week.\""}, "C36" {:src "\"Another loading view taking the same load: each person's days booked and working days over the weeks shown.\""}, "C37" {:src "\"A block taking two capacities: what the relaunch leaves (left) and the calendar alone (calendar), told apart by their names: each is bound to the one named as it is.\""}, "C38" {:src "\"A block: the Scheduler's plan worked out again many times, each task's work drawn between its Low and High in Tasks, most often its Work, so it says how likely each finish is. It takes Tasks, and the Scheduler itself, which it calls.\""}, "C4" {:src "\"The plan's last day: the Scheduler block's plan.\""}, "C5" {:src "\"When the latest baseline was taken: the one the Baseline block gives, which Tracking follows.\""}, "C6" {:src "\"The last day of the latest baseline.\""}, "C7" {:src "\"Working days between the baseline's finish and the forecast, on the Working calendar block's calendar.\""}, "C8" {:src "\"Done, weighted by each task's work.\""}, "C9" {:src "\"Earned value over planned value at the status date.\""}}, :values {"A1" "Website relaunch", "A10" "Cost performance (CPI)", "A11" "Tasks late on the baseline", "A12" "Critical path", "A13" "Double-booked days", "A14" "Overbooked weeks", "A15" "Earned value", "A16" "Assignments to check", "A17" "Settings", "A18" "Start", "A19" "Status date", "A2" "Summary", "A20" "Level resources", "A21" "Data", "A22" "Resources", "A23" "Tasks", "A24" "Roles", "A25" "Blocks", "A26" "Working calendar", "A27" "Timesheet", "A28" "Scheduler", "A29" "Baselines", "A3" "Status date", "A30" "Tracking", "A31" "Gantt", "A3